;.
  ;@ /flow/definition web_source_guide
  ;= Maintain a guide from web sources

    Bind urls to ordinary records with a url text slot, one record per source.
    Changing a bound record creates a new request. A revision slot can explicitly
    request a fresh capture without changing its URL. There is no polling loop.
    Captures and failures remain attached to this invocation. An unavailable
    source leaves unresolved work and cannot become current source evidence.

    This procedure performs bounded HTTP GET requests through the native foot.
    Markdown sources decompose into headings and native concept documents.
    Other supported text is retained as literal evidence; interpreting HTML or
    structured registry responses requires an explicitly authored next step.

    ;@ /flow/input urls
    ;= Named web sources

    ;@ /flow/step fetched ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/web_fetch
    ;@ /flow/bind urls urls
    ;= Capture each requested web source

    ;@ /flow/step sources ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/web_sources
    ;@ /flow/bind responses fetched
    ;= Use only successful retained captures

    ;@ /flow/step checked ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/inventory
    ;@ /flow/bind sources sources
    ;= Validate native provenance

    ;@ /flow/step decomposed ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/decompose
    ;@ /flow/bind sources checked
    ;= Decompose source structure

    ;@ /flow/step pages ;/0x11/gov/flows/operations/documents
    ;@ /flow/bind pages document
    ;@ /flow/bind sources decomposed
    ;= Compose the source guide

    ;@ /flow/result pages
    ;= Publish through the existing guarded writer

    ;@ /flow/page /
    ;= Web source guide

      The reference children come from captured HTTP responses. Their native
      result references identify the retained evidence; URLs identify where it
      was requested. This page does not assert that an old capture is current.
